quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  7,52,"We have indeed brought them a Book which We have expounded with knowledge, as a guidance and a mercy for a people who believe."
  7,53,"Do they wait for anything except the fulfilment of this (warning)? The Day when (the moment of) its fulfilment comes, those who had forgotten it before will say: ‘The messengers of Our Lord had certainly brought the truth. Are there any intercessors for us (now) who can intercede on our behalf? Or could we be sent back to do other than what we used to do?’ They have surely ruined their souls, and whatever (false beliefs and idols) they used to invent will abandon them."
  7,54,"Indeed, your Lord is Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth in six periods and then settled (His Might) on the Throne (i.e. enforced His command and power over the universe). He causes the night to cover the day, pursuing it rapidly. And (He created) the sun, moon and stars (all) subjected to His command. Surely, all creation and command belong to Him. Blessed is Allah, the Lord of all worlds."
  7,55,"Supplicate your Lord humbly and secretly. Indeed, He does not like the transgressors."
  7,56,"Do not cause corruption on the earth after it has been set in order. And supplicate Him with fear and hope. Indeed, Allah’s mercy is close to the virtuously excellent."
  7,57,"He is the One Who sends the winds bearing good news before (the showering of) His mercy. When they have gathered up the heavy clouds, We drive them towards a dead land, where We cause rain to fall. Then We bring out with it all kinds of crops. Thus shall We bring out the dead (to life). Perhaps you may be mindful (of advice)."
